From 2e97cc851247da83abd6abc5d03a95213738e7bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sivasubramaniyan Padmanaban <sivasubramaniyan.padmanaban@analog.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:59:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] tegra234 overlay: move ADSD3500/ADTF3066 to serial_c, drop
 RGB node

- Reassign all ADSD3500/ADTF3066 sensor modes from serial_b to serial_c
CSI interface, dropping the now-unneeded lane_polarity override.
- Remove the i2c@1 arducam@0c RGB sensor node and its CSI input
endpoint entirely; simplify the ADSD3500 CSI output endpoint
(adsd3500_out0->out1, drop port-index/bus-width/remote-endpoint).
- Replace GPIO hog output-high entries with explicit pinmux
tristate/pull/lpdr/function=rsvd2 configuration.

Signed-off-by: Sivasubramaniyan Padmanaban <sivasubramaniyan.padmanaban@analog.com>
---
 ...p3768-adsd3500-adtf3066-arducam-ar0234.dts | 587 +++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 220 insertions(+), 367 deletions(-)

